course: dictionary
lesson: 2020
title: Many meanings: conference
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. To find the right one, read the words around it. Those words are the context, and they leave clues.
explain: «At parent–teacher conferences, your parents and teacher talk about how you are doing.» Here a conference is a smaller meeting about one subject: you. The words parent and teacher tell you who is meeting.
explain: «At the Berlin Conference of 1884 and 1885 European powers agreed rules for dividing Africa among themselves, and no African was in the room.» Here a conference is a big, formal meeting where many people come together to discuss something important. Check it by swapping in meeting: it still makes sense.
fact: A conference is a meeting where people come together to discuss or learn about a subject.
fact: A big conference can last one day or more, and many people attend it.
fact: A parent–teacher conference is a smaller meeting to talk about a child's progress. In the UK it is often called «parents' evening».
fact: A press conference is when leaders answer reporters' questions.
fact: In US sport, a conference is a group of teams that play against each other.
exercise: «At parent–teacher conferences, your parents and teacher talk about how you are doing.» What is a conference here? | A test you take alone | A race between two teams | *A meeting to talk about something important | A football match at the park
exercise: «The scientists shared their discoveries at a conference that lasted three days.» How long did the conference last? | Three minutes | Half a second | Three hours | *Three days
exercise: Which phrase means a meeting where a leader answers reporters' questions? | Parent–teacher conference | Dinner party | *Press conference | Video conference
test: In US sport, what is a conference? | *A group of teams that play against each other | A big formal meeting about rules | A kind of school bell | A small chat with a teacher
test: «At the Berlin Conference of 1884 and 1885, no African was in the room.» What does this suggest about who was at the meeting? | *Only European powers, not African people | Only children from the school | Only the reporters | Everyone from Africa and Europe
exam: Which sentence best describes a conference? | A piece of music played at a party | A kind of fast animal | A long walk in the countryside | *A big or small meeting where people come together to discuss or learn about something
